entries.definition_en:
ὑακίνθος, -ου, ό 
 [in LXX chiefly for תְּכֵלֶת ;] 
hyacinth; 
 __(a) in cl., a flower, prob. the dark blue iris; 
 __(b) in late writers, a precious stone of the same colour, perhaps the sapphire: Rev.21:20 (Phil., FlJ, al.).†
 (AS)

A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.10; 
 son of: Bilhan (H1092H); 
 brother of: Jeush (H3266H), Benjamin (H1144H), Ehud (H0164H), Chenaanah (H3668H), Tarshish (H8659I) and Ahishahar (H0300) 
 § Zethan = "olive"
 a Benjamite of the sons of Bilhan

A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.3.19; 
 son of: Pedaiah (H6305H); 
 brother of: Shimei (H8096J); 
 father of: Meshullam (H4918H), Hananiah (H2608L), Shelomith (H8019I), Hashubah (H2807), Ohel (H0169), Berechiah (H1296), Hasadiah (H2619), Jushab-hesed (H3142) and Abiud (G0010); also called Sheshbazzar at Ezr.1.8,11; 5.14,16; KJV: Zorobabel at Mat.1.12,13;
Aramaic of ze.rub.ba.vel (זְרֻבָּבֶ֫ל "Zerubbabel" H2216) 
 § Zerubbabel = "sown in Babylon"
 the grandson of king Jehoiachin and leader of the first group of returning exiles from Babylon
